comment:
Last year, between back pain, living on my own and having had surgery, I picked up a countertop diswasher not too dissimilar from the one shown here; I'm renting and don't have the space for anything bigger so it was fairly perfect, I do have to drain the unit into a mob bucket (the mop handle holder is the perfect retainer for the drain pipe) but, it generally works well;

I do have two larger plates that I have to put at the edge of the unit otherwise it blocks the sprayer, I also didn't get a cutlery box thing, mine just uses the shelf with some lift up retainers which is somewhat annoying but works until I somehow end up with much more cutlery than dishes in there; It is nice because I can put stuff in there over the course of the day and turn it on over night. I will note that the shelf can be lowered a bit which is how they get cups on the top.

Volume is really the big issue with these things, but, it beats having nothing and takes up a space in the kitchen which would have only been used by something like an air fryer than can sit on my main work surface without being in the way much; sadly have to wash cook ware seperatly, be that manually or on a 2nd wash, but, it is at least a better situation than I was in before.
